    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d508">

                <pb facs="0629" n="615" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg615"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.1216M/2342</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Mr. Charles A. Timm of the Division of
                        the American Republics to the Adviser on Political Relations</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Duggan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-05-22">May 22, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Duggan</hi>: The attached letter from Mr.
                        Lawson<anchor n="53" xml:id="d508-f1"/> tends to justify our firm position
                    here on the Mexicali situation.</p>
                <p>There is some reason to believe, and I suspect Mr. Lawson has this in view, that
                    certain Mexicans may be trying to induce us to set the precedent of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">assuring</hi> the delivery of a greater amount of water
                    than we now contemplate allocating by treaty. It would seem that both the
                    Imperial District and the Mexicans need careful watching.</p>
                <p>It may be that a letter asking these specific questions should be sent to Mr.
                    Lawson: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Are the Mexicali lands actually getting enough water?</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Has the Mexican Commissioner specifically advised the Foreign Office
                            that no real shortage exists?</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Is there any real danger of a shortage during this growing
                            season?</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>Should it become necessary or possible to take over the facilities
                            below Pilot Knob,<anchor n="54" xml:id="d508-f2"/> would the American
                            Section be in a position immediately to operate them?</item>
                    </list></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d508-f1" n="53" xml:id="d508-f1-content">
                <p>Letter dated May 21 from Mr. Lawson to the Secretary of State, not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d508-f2" n="54" xml:id="d508-f2-content">
                <p>A spillway or diversion dam in the Colorado River above Yuma.</p>
            </note>
